          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\begin{aligned}f(x)&=2x-3\\\\g(x)&=\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p140-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the domain and range of $g(f(x))$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Domain: $\\left[\\frac{3}{2},\\infty\\right)$. Range: $[0,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(f(x))&=g(2x-3)\\\\g(f(x))&=\\sqrt{2x-3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe inner function $f$ accepts every real input. The outer square root requires\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-3&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus the domain is $\\left[\\frac{3}{2},\\infty\\right)$. On this domain, $2x-3$ takes every value in $[0,\\infty)$, so its square root also takes every value in $[0,\\infty)$.\n\nRange: $[0,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p140-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the domain and range of $f(g(x))$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Domain: $[0,\\infty)$. Range: $[-3,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=f(\\sqrt{x})\\\\f(g(x))&=2\\sqrt{x}-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe inner square root requires $x\\ge0$. The outer function $f$ accepts every real input, so there is no further restriction.\n\nDomain: $[0,\\infty)$.\n\nFor $x\\ge0$, $\\sqrt{x}$ takes every non-negative value. Therefore $2\\sqrt{x}-3$ takes every value from $-3$ upwards, including $-3$ when $x=0$.\n\nRange: $[-3,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
